cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper below."
title: "Temporal Conditioning for Human Behavioral Cloning in Chess"
abstract: >-
  A time-aware chess transformer that extends a Chessformer-style architecture
  with learned temporal conditioning tokens encoding player clock state, time
  control and recent tempo, together with behavioral heads for thinking time and
  resignation. Temporal conditioning yields modest overall move-matching gains
  that concentrate sharply under time pressure, and lets the sampled policy
  reproduce the human move-quality degradation that time-blind behavioral cloning
  models systematically underestimate.
